					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/neghtasro" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2166522); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2166522&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606274105" alt="Neghtasro" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2166522)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/neghtasro" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2166522); return false;" >Neghtasro</a></span> <span class="odate time_1436884276 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">14 Jul 2015 14:31</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2337823">
									

<p>I think you've got a decent idea here, but there's a few things keeping me from upvoting.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Fortunately as with most NASA missions, public interest is sufficiently low, so it is considered to be of little risk.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't like this line. Tonally, it's off, and while I get that this whole thing has a sense of tongue-in-cheek throughout, this just pushes it a bit too far.</p>
<p>I'm also not sold on the containment procedures. It's done, Pluto is gone. Why would the Foundation perpetually sink resources into keeping everyone thinking it's there when they could say something like &quot;New Horizons has detected a large object on a collision course with Pluto coming from the outer Kuiper Belt&quot; and transition to the contingency plan within in the next few years? Better to get it out of the way now than wait until civilian technology has advanced to the point where they start asking questions so they have to say &quot;Oh yeah, that blew up last year, sorry we forgot to bring it up&quot;?</p>
<p>Other than that, I'm not overly fond of the fact that your hook is in the last three sentences, but that's probably a personal thing. I mostly like this, but those things are keeping me from upvoting right now.</p>

							</div>

								
					
